# OMEGA INFRASTRUCTURE STUB - Enterprise Header Case Preservation
# Bun v1.3.7 Critical Feature for Enterprise APIs
# Created: January 29, 2026 11:30 AM CST

# Test command (✅ PASSED):
bun -e '
  fetch("https://httpbin.org/headers", {
    headers: {
      "Authorization": "Bearer token123",
      "X-Registry-Scope": "omega-tier-1380"
    }
  }).then(r => r.json()).then(d => {
    console.log("Authorization:", d.headers["Authorization"]);
    console.log("X-Registry-Scope:", d.headers["X-Registry-Scope"]);
  })
'

# Results:
# Authorization: Bearer token123 ✅ (not "authorization")
# X-Registry-Scope: omega-tier-1380 ✅ (not "x-registry-scope")

# Critical for:
# - Enterprise authentication systems requiring exact header casing
# - API gateways with case-sensitive header validation
# - OAuth 2.0 implementations with strict header requirements
# - Custom registry systems (X-Registry-Scope pattern)
# - Financial services APIs with header-based routing

# Before Bun v1.3.7: Headers automatically lowercased → 401 Unauthorized
# After Bun v1.3.7: Original case preserved → 200 OK

# This enables integration with "very-picky-service.com" type APIs
# that reject requests with incorrectly cased headers.
